ight track in May 1978  Ben and Jerry's homemade ice cream  parlor opened up what was previously an  abandoned gas station that they've  renovated using 8,000 dollars of their  own money and $4,000 borrowed by  creating unusual but tasty flavors like  Chubby Hubby and the 14 thousand calorie  ver monster which was Greenfields job to  manufacture and sponsoring community  events  word of the store quickly spread  throughout the town by the end of 1984  Ben and Jerry's had sales in excess of  four million dollars double the figure  from the previous year by 1999 the  company's total revenue was 237 million  dollars through a strategy of engaging  in social activism and corporate social  responsibility and using all-natural  ingredients for their products Ben and  Jerry's stood out in a highly  competitive industry in 2000 the company  and its franchises were acquired by  Unilever for 326 million dollars by  following their passion for the food  industry and by believing in their  socially conscious ideals Ben and Jerry  really do go from a five dollar course  and wrenching an abandoned gas station  into building a well known brand and  being acquired for over three hundred  million dollars to help you copy their  success here are the top three action  items and you can learn from Ben &amp; Jerry  action item number one behave  responsibly if you look at any lasting  and successful company you'll see that  they have a set of core values that they  really believe in it helps guide the  decisions and also tracks employees and  customers who believe the same way one  example of a core value is behaving  responsibly do you believe that your  business should exist not just to serve  your customers but also to serve the  greater community if yes you should  incorporate this message into everything  you do so people know about it and will  be attracted to your business Ben &amp;  Jerry's has become famous not only for  his unique and delicious flavors of ice  cream but also f